## Why This Problem Is Asked
This problem combines prefix DP with an inner backward sweep to compute the optimal segment ending at each position. It tests understanding of state decomposition, reconstruction logic, and handles edge cases like negative values naturally.

## Key Concepts
- DP state: dp[i][t] tracks the optimal value using the first i elements with t segments
- Inner loop: expanding the left boundary computes segment maximum on the fly
- Reconstruction: store predecessor pointers to recover exact subarray boundaries
- Complexity: O(n²k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueSubarrays(A, k) {
    const n = A.length;
    const dp = Array(n + 1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
    const prev = Array(n + 1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
    dp[0][0] = 0;

    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
            let curMax = -Infinity;
            for (let l = i; l >= 1; l--) {
                curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[l - 1]);
                const val = (dp[l - 1][t - 1] !== -Infinity ? dp[l - 1][t - 1] + curMax : -Infinity);
                if (val > dp[i][t]) {
                    dp[i][t] = val;
                    prev[i][t] = l;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    const result = [];
    let i = n, t = k;
    while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
        const l = prev[i][t];
        result.unshift([l, i]);
        i = l - 1;
        t--;
    }
    return { value: dp[n][k], boundaries: result };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a three-dimensional DP that models constrained path planning with a binary obstacle grid and a budget of unblocks. Requires careful state definition, transitions, and path reconstruction. 

## Key Concepts
- DP with an extra dimension for unblocks (t)
- Handling blocked vs unblocked cells in transitions
- Path reconstruction from 3D DP table
- Time/space trade-offs and rolling optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPath(grid, blocked, k) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: m}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG)));
  if (!blocked[0][0]) dp[0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  else if (k > 0) dp[0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
        const val = grid[i][j];
        if (i > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t] + val * (blocked[i][j] ? 0 : 1));
          if (blocked[i][j] && t > 0) dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t-1] + val);
        }
        if (j > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t] + val * (blocked[i][j] ? 0 : 1));
          if (blocked[i][j] && t > 0) dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t-1] + val);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[n-1][m-1][0];
}
```

