## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests DP formulation for selecting multiple non-overlapping subarrays with reconstruction—a common pattern in budget allocation and resource optimization scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- **DP over prefixes and block counts**: State `dp[i][t]` tracks the optimal solution using only the first i elements for exactly t blocks.
- **Prefix sums**: Enable O(1) computation of any subarray sum as `pref[r] - pref[l-1]`.
- **Backpointers**: Store decision history to reconstruct the actual subarray boundaries after computing the DP table.
- **Time/space complexity**: Baseline O(n²k) time and O(nk) space; can be optimized with divide-and-conquer or convex hull tricks for larger inputs.

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i - 1] + A[i - 1];

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const choice = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(k + 1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      choice[i][t] = { type: 'skip', i: i - 1 };

      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const val = dp[s - 1][t - 1] + pref[i] - pref[s - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          choice[i][t] = { type: 'start', s, i };
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct boundaries
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const c = choice[i][t];
    if (c.type === 'start') {
      blocks.unshift([c.s, c.i]);
      i = c.s - 1;
    } else {
      i = c.i;
    }
    t--;
  }

  return { maxSum: dp[n][k], boundaries: blocks };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP design for selecting multiple disjoint subarrays with reconstruction. Requires prefix sums, state definition, and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- DP over positions and count of subarrays
- Prefix sums for subarray sums
- Reconstructing intervals with predecessor pointers
- Time/space trade-offs (O(nk) vs optimizations)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length; const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const from = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>new Array(k+1).fill(null));
  for (let i=0;i<=n;i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  for (let t=1;t<=k;t++){
    let best = -Infinity;
    let bestIdx = -1;
    for (let i=1;i<=n;i++){
      if (dp[i-1][t-1] - P[i-1] > best){ best = dp[i-1][t-1] - P[i-1]; bestIdx = i-1; }
      const take = P[i] + best;
      if (take > dp[i-1][t]){ dp[i][t] = take; from[i][t] = [bestIdx+1, i]; }
      else { dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t]; }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction (omitted for brevity in this snippet)
  return {maxSum: dp[n][k], intervals: []};
}
```

